        "original_id": "14bfb241-1a5d-5e98-ad5d-4be5a14cfad7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sergei Sobolev, Mikhail Gromov, Nikolay Brusentsov\n- Organizations: IHÉS, New York University\n- Products: Setun\n- Topics: mathematical analysis, partial differential equations, geometry, group theory\n\nFacts:\n- Sergei Sobolev was born on 6 October 1908 and died on 3 January 1989.\n- Sergei Sobolev was a Soviet mathematician who worked in mathematical analysis and partial differential equations.\n- Mikhail Gromov was born on 23 December 1943.\n- Mikhail Gromov is a French-Russian mathematician known for work in geometry, analysis, and group theory.\n- Mikhail Gromov is a permanent member of IHÉS in France and a Professor of Mathematics at New York University.\n- Setun was built under the leadership of Sergei Sobolev and Nikolay Brusentsov.",
